  "reasoning": "According to established molecular biology and guidance from global health authorities (including the CDC, WHO, and NIH), mRNA COVID-19 vaccines cannot alter or interact with human DNA. The mRNA delivered by the vaccine operates entirely within the cytoplasm of the cell, where ribosomes translate it into the target viral spike protein. It never enters the cell nucleus where genetic material (DNA) is kept. Furthermore, human cells do not possess the enzymes (such as reverse transcriptase and integrase) required to reverse-transcribe synthetic mRNA into DNA and integrate it into the human genome. The vaccine mRNA is fragile and is naturally degraded and cleared by normal cellular processes shortly after being translated.",
